Paired-cube causal operation-frame search
Apache-2.0, following the repository license.
Prepared with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance.

This package checks new operation frames for the PR168 bit word. All construction, partner-pair decoder, carrier matching, gauge, source-sharing, frame compiler, complex supplier, paid moment, row-stock, atom-toll and balanced-layout lineage in the repository notices remains credited to the original authors.

The selected initial.json is Joel Pulikkan's (GamingPuzzled) PR169 replacement-frames.json at commit 4895ba1104cedc7908b6d6ba64fdd6290e0ed7ae, prepared with Anthropic Claude assistance and released under Apache-2.0. PR169 credits Chafik Boukhalfa's (chafreaky) PR165 replacement format, checker and prime witnesses, with frame descent from PR163/PR164 and the frame lemma from PR130/PR131. Those physical-frame ascent/descent ideas and the supplied initial plan are not claimed as new here.

This package refines the supplied plan using causal prefix descents and suffix ascents, alternating them against the complete paid boundary moment with exact rational acceptance. It checks the exported physical frames independently, without assuming that an improved frame must be a subspace of its original operation frame. The selected search accepts 240 downward moves and 120 upward moves from the credited PR169 start.

word.py, interval_moment.py and moment.py adapt the finite formal-column and exact arithmetic implementations in PR163; prime_check.py retains PR164's Bareiss determinant and prime-factor proof. The original authors and OpenAI Codex assistance credited by those packages remain acknowledged. The search changes no scalar operations, gauges, root schedules or source mixing. No prerequisite construction or inherited all-size theorem is claimed as new. A finite supplier improvement alone is not a final multiplication-bound certificate.
